# Build-context filter for Rust worker images -- the template/fallback copy.
#
# Copy this to `<workspace>/.dockerignore`. Only a file with that exact name,
# sitting at an ancestor of the copied sources, is honoured when the SDK hashes
# the image tag (see `_ignore_file_for` in _image.py); this packaged copy filters
# the uploaded build context but not the hash.
#
# NOTE: supplying a .dockerignore REPLACES the SDK's standard ignore patterns,
# so everything to exclude must be listed here.
target
**/target
.git
**/.git
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
# The worker image builds Rust only; excluding Python keeps launcher edits from
# invalidating the image tag. Both forms: a bare pattern matches only the context
# root, as with `target` / `**/target` above.
*.py
**/*.py
.venv
**/.venv
.flyte
**/.flyte
.DS_Store
